    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 122210\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n310 PM PDT Mon Oct 12 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms expected to continue \n  through the day today.\n\n* A cold front will push through the region tonight, bringing\n  gusty northwest winds and much cooler temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Sunday.\n\nMoisture associated with the remnants of Rachel continues to linger \nacross the forecast area today, with scattered showers and isolated \nthunderstorms possible across southeastern California, southern \nNevada, and northwestern Arizona. Chances decrease across our \nsouthern zones after sunset, with persistent chances of showers and \nthunderstorms in the southern Great Basin overnight. In general, \nrain rates should remain light-to-moderate, though with thunderstorm \nformation, can't rule out locally heavy rainfall. Soils are \nsaturated across the region from heavy rain experienced yesterday. \nAs a result, it is likely that any moderate-to-heavy rain that falls \ntoday will cause nuisance ponding and/or isolated instances of flash \nflooding. Sprinkles-to-light rain possible through Tuesday morning \nbefore skies begin to clear and the region dries out. \n\nAn upper-level trough and associated cold front will push \nsoutheastward through the forecast area tonight, bringing with it \ngusty northwest winds and much cooler temperatures. Gusty winds will \npeak Tuesday morning across northern Inyo, Esmeralda, and central \nNye counties, with gust speeds between 30 and 40 mph. Northwesterly \nwinds will spread through the whole forecast area through the day, \nwith speeds between 20 and 30 mph. These winds (encouraging mixing \nof warmer air above the surface), coupled with cloud cover sticking \naround through the first portion of the overnight period (trapping \nwarm air at the surface beneath them) will likely prevent Bishop \nfrom freezing tonight. As a result, have cancelled the Freeze Watch \nfor the northern Owens Valley and reissued it for Tuesday night into \nWednesday morning, when winds have subsided and skies have cleared. \nThe Freeze Watch for Esmeralda and central Nye tonight into Tuesday \nmorning looks good and has been upgraded to a Freeze Warning. \nTemperatures will bottom out across the region on Tuesday, with \nhighs for desert valleys in the upper-60s to low-70s. Temperatures \nwill gradually climb through the remainder of the work week into the \nweekend.\n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package... \nScattered showers remain possible through early evening in the Las \nVegas Valley vicinity with brief rainfall and CIGS in the 7-8kft AGL \nrange as they move through. Otherwise, partly cloudy skies are \nexpected with decreasing cloud cover overnight. Southwesterly winds \nwith gusts of around 25 knots are expected through the evening \nbefore decreasing overnight. A weak cold front will drop south early \nTuesday morning, arriving in the Las Vegas Valley between 14-16z \nwith a wind shift to the north expected with gusts of 20-25 knots. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Scattered showers and \nisolated thunderstorms will continue to be possible across the \neastern half of the region this afternoon, potentially resulting in \nimpacts at all regional TAF sites except KDAG. Breezy southwesterly \nwinds are expected as well before decreasing after dark. Exception \nwill be near KBIH where a cold front will move through this evening \nshifting the winds to a northerly direction. This shift will spread \nsouth earth Tuesday, with northerly winds reaching the Colorado \nRiver Valley after 16z. &&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat\nAVIATION...Outler\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
